{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/951403-example-nameless-orders","id":951403,"title":"Example Nameless Orders","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-15T17:49:30-07:00","id":951403,"title":"Example Nameless Orders","content":"Heya.<br /> <br /> I've been planning to write some setting stuff regarding Mage for my personal use. Among the things I've been planning to do something with were Nameless Orders.<br /> I always liked the alternate Covenants of Vampire and Changeling's new Court system fits my style perfectly, which makes me interested in Mage's own more local factions.<br /> I'd like to hear about some of the Nameless Orders that you guys might have used, to help me find inspiration for my own.<br /> <br /> As well as that, I'd like to know if there are any books with information on Nameless Orders from First Edition.<br /> Thanks to anyone who responds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T18:00:08-07:00","id":951409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/898221-2e-insert-nameless-orders-here\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/898221-2e-insert-nameless-orders-here\"> [2E] Insert Nameless Orders Here - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/898221-2e-insert-nameless-orders-here\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/898221-2e-insert-nameless-orders-here </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> This one is pretty straightforward. Post any Nameless Orders you've made or translated for Second Edition. I'll start with one of mine. The Epistolary Society of </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T18:06:42-07:00","id":951411,"title":"","content":"There are also some Nameless Orders that maintain an identity be being cocooned into the big Orders but maintaining ties across them. The Elemental Tamers for instance function like that (Legacies the Ancient). The Tremere are a Nameless Order as well (Left Hand Path). The Seers kind of have a butt load of them, they all wave the Seer flag but there are secret splinter cells that serve &quot;lesser&quot; Exarchs in the hopes of raising them to ascendancy and taking over the Iron Pyramid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T09:49:59-07:00","id":951787,"title":"","content":"The Porcerlain Ring consists of several intertwined Chinese proximi families, most of which migrated to Manila in the early to mid-19th century from Fujian Province and other parts of southern China. Though Awakenings among the Ring have become rare, their Sleepwalkers still have access to a wide variety of charms, imbued items, and grimoires. Moreover, their combined clout in the business world allows them resources and leverage lesser Nameless Orders could only dream of.<br /> <br /> To this end, the Porcelain Ring has 2 goals: <br /> <br /> 1) To maintain and safeguard Manila's grey market for Awakened needs: Powdered Seraph feathers, herbs from the Primal Wild, tiger bone Tass, and everything in between. Both Pentacle and Seer parties are forbidden from antagonizing each other while in Porcelain grounds.<br /> <br /> 2) To depose their rivals: Jiangshi elders who control large family corporations from the shadows. Both the Ring and the Chinese Kindred wage proxy wars via corporate espionage, gang warfare, and the drug trade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4260,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","user":"terpsichordean","date":". 08-16-2016, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}